<title>FRANCE: CLF sees rise in profits in 1996.</title>
<headline>CLF sees rise in profits in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Credit Local de France forecast on Wednesday another rise in profit for full-year 1996 after reporting a six percent increase in half-year earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;Credit Local de France expects a further increase in its profits in 1996, a (profit) growth uninterrupted since its creation in 1987,&quot; bank chairman Pierre Richard said.</p>
<p>He made the forecast in a statement showing that first half-net attributable profit rose to 793 million francs from 748 million.</p>
</text>
